  "step_2": "The individual states that the difference in probability is only 1%, which they perceive as nearly identical, and therefore they choose the option with more money (2500 Euros vs. 2400 Euros). The individual does not mention skewness, asymmetry, or any consideration of the distribution of outcomes. Their justification is based solely on the amount of money offered and the minimal difference in probabilities. There is no reference to unfavorable outcomes, probability distribution shape, or skewness in the deliberation process.",
  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason—specifically, that lottery A is more right-skewed due to a higher probability (67%) of the unfavorable 0 Euro outcome—is not considered by the individual. The individual does not mention skewness or distributional asymmetry at all. Instead, the justification is based purely on the higher monetary value and negligible difference in probabilities. The decision reason's rule (prefer the more right-skewed lottery) is not reflected in the reported deliberation. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason to make the decision.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

